------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  'random' is the causal control: identical entry rule, direction thrown
  away. It is the only row where nothing but the forecast differs, so it
  is the one that isolates the model's contribution.

  The other rows are competing STRATEGIES with their own entry rules and
  their own trade sets. Losing to one of them can mean the signal is worse
  OR that the model picks costlier trades -- compare gross/trade against
  cost/trade before deciding which.

  And when every strategy loses money, 'which loses least' is a weak
  ranking: not trading at all scores $0 and beats all of them.
